Chapter: DeskMonBlockTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The Monitor's `input` row comes out of its own block, and an unwritten block
 reads as a plausible wrong answer rather than as an error.

 That row is the one fact this pane's tree cannot reach for itself.
 `desk-wnd-paint-all` is handed the screen and `ds`, so `kbd` and `mouse` are
 not in scope where the tree is built; `desk-mon-open` writes whether each was
 enumerated into the block instead. A block nobody wrote reads zero, and zero
 is `mailbox` and `no` -- which is exactly what a machine with no USB HID
 keyboard and no mouse reports, so the failure is a pane confidently saying
 the hardware is absent. Nothing about the picture says which it is.

 So the arm is the DIFFERENCE and not either arm alone: the same tree built
 over a written block and an unwritten one must not read the same. A
 `dk-mon-tree` that stopped consulting the block at all would answer one
 string under both, which is what this file exists to refuse.

 The other rows are not asserted. They are the machine talking about itself
 and every one of them moves with the box, the build and the second; the
 `input` row is the only one whose value this chapter puts there. What IS
 asserted about them is that three of the eleven keys are present, which is
 what catches a row deleted or renamed while the pane still paints.

 SABOTAGED by answering the row from literals rather than from the block, the
 two readings become `keyboard USB HID   mouse yes` and `they differ` goes to
 no. Nothing else in the file moves, and nothing about the pane on the screen
 would have looked wrong.

Section: Test

 A label's text is in its KIND rather than in a field of its own, so reading
 one back is two matches and not a projection.

  mb-kind-text : WidgetNode -> Text
  mb-kind-text (n) =
    when n.wn-kind
      is WkLabel (t) -> t
      is otherwise -> "<not a label>"

  mb-text : WidgetNode, Text -> Text
  mb-text (tree) (id) =
    when widget-find tree id
      is Just (n) -> mb-kind-text n
      is None -> "<absent>"

  mb-ds : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mb-ds (kbd) (mouse) =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let gp = poke-32 ds desk-gpu-cell 1
    in let mp = poke-32 ds dk-mon-cell (alloc-zeroed 64 64)
    in let blk = peek-32 ds dk-mon-cell
    in let k = poke-32 blk dk-mon-kbd-cell kbd
    in let m = poke-32 blk dk-mon-mouse-cell mouse
    in ds

  mb-yn : Boolean -> Text
  mb-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ai = acpi-boot 0
    in let written = mb-ds 1 1
    in let unwritten = mb-ds 0 0
    in let tw = dk-mon-tree written 3204448256 1600 900 1600 gfont-none ai "00:00:00" 0
    in let tu = dk-mon-tree unwritten 3204448256 1600 900 1600 gfont-none ai "00:00:00" 0
    in let vw = mb-text tw "mon-v-input"
    in let vu = mb-text tu "mon-v-input"
    in act
      print-line-uni ("written   " & vw)
      print-line-uni ("unwritten " & vu)
      print-line-uni ("they differ: " & mb-yn (vw /= vu))
      print-line-uni ("rows " & mb-text tw "mon-k-display" & " " & mb-text tw "mon-k-memory" & " " & mb-text tw "mon-k-stack")
      print-line-uni ("title " & desk-wnd-title desk-focus-mon & "  block " & mb-yn (desk-wnd-blk desk-focus-mon written == peek-32 written dk-mon-cell))
    end

